       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. A single 5,000 mg dose is also well above the ~75\u2013150 mg/kg range associated with hepatotoxicity risk for a 70 kg patient (about 71 mg/kg). That's a potentially fatal overdose, even with normal liver and kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **5000 mg/day total**, which is still over the limit and would need to be lowered\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want the 5,000 mg dose, please tell me the clinical reason. I'd still want to confirm it with pharmacy before entering it."
      }
